---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CaseStudyHeader from '../../components/CaseStudyHeader.astro';
import EvidencePanel from '../../components/EvidencePanel.astro';
import ContactCTA from '../../components/ContactCTA.astro';

const facts = [
  { num: '12', lbl: 'Consecutive dated weekly reports through 19 October 2026' },
  { num: '127', lbl: 'Structured history records in the audited log' },
  { num: '18', lbl: 'Individually verified opportunities in the most recent audited cycle' },
  { num: '1', lbl: 'Beneficiary — not a commercial multi-tenant deployment' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Turning recurring research into a verifiable workflow — Fabio Valente"
  description="Case study: scheduled opportunity-research automation with profile-based filters, source verification, structured history, and weekly reporting."
>
  <CaseStudyHeader
    num="02"
    title="Turning recurring research into a verifiable workflow"
    status="BUSINESS AUTOMATION / OPERATIONAL PRIVATE WORKFLOW"
    lead="A recurring research task combined searching, screening, verifying sources, maintaining history, and reporting useful findings. I designed the workflow requirements and operated an AI-assisted research assistant to perform the repeatable work and make uncertainty visible."
  >
    <div class="facts-row">
      {facts.map((f) => (
        <div class="fact">
          <div class="num">{f.num}</div>
          <div class="lbl">{f.lbl}</div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </CaseStudyHeader>

  <div class="container case-body">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Problem</h2>
      <p>
        Manual opportunity screening was repetitive, time-sensitive, and prone to duplication. A
        useful automation needed to remember past findings, enforce eligibility and compensation
        filters, check links and source claims, and distinguish inaccessible pages from verified
        openings.
      </p>

      <h2>My role</h2>
      <p>
        I defined the beneficiary profile, language and compensation filters, acceptance criteria,
        report format, source-verification rules, and operational review process. I monitored the
        output and continuity. AI agents authored the underlying scripts and executed source
        searches.
      </p>

      <h2>Workflow</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Scheduled weekly trigger.</li>
        <li>Load stored profile and previous-history entries.</li>
        <li>Discover candidate opportunities using configured sources.</li>
        <li>Filter on relevant role, location/eligibility, compensation when available, and duplicates.</li>
        <li>Verify direct source pages individually; mark failures and inaccessible pages.</li>
        <li>Write updated CSV/history.</li>
        <li>Generate an actionable, dated report.</li>
        <li>Deliver to Discord; record issues and the next cycle's state.</li>
      </ol>

      <div class="diagram-panel">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 680 210" role="img" aria-label="Workflow diagram: schedule loads profile and history, discovers candidates, filters, verifies sources, records results, and reports to Discord. Unverified or access-blocked items branch separately instead of being counted as verified.">
          <defs>
            <marker id="arr2" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="6" refY="3" orient="auto">
              <path d="M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 Z" fill="#3E5C76"></path>
            </marker>
          </defs>
          <style>
            .n2 { fill:#FFFFFF; stroke:#C9CFD6; }
            .b2 { fill:#F7F1E6; stroke:#8A6D3B; }
            .t2 { fill:#23282E; font:600 12.5px Manrope,sans-serif; }
            .s2 { fill:#7A7F86; font:500 9.5px 'IBM Plex Mono',monospace; letter-spacing:.06em; }
            .a2 { stroke:#3E5C76; stroke-width:1.5; fill:none; }
          </style>
          <rect class="n2" x="10" y="30" width="90" height="52" rx="8"></rect>
          <text class="t2" x="55" y="51" text-anchor="middle">Schedule</text>
          <text class="s2" x="55" y="66" text-anchor="middle">WEEKLY</text>
          <path class="a2" d="M100,56 L118,56" marker-end="url(#arr2)"></path>

          <rect class="n2" x="120" y="30" width="100" height="52" rx="8"></rect>
          <text class="t2" x="170" y="51" text-anchor="middle">Profile</text>
          <text class="s2" x="170" y="66" text-anchor="middle">+ HISTORY</text>
          <path class="a2" d="M220,56 L238,56" marker-end="url(#arr2)"></path>

          <rect class="n2" x="240" y="30" width="90" height="52" rx="8"></rect>
          <text class="t2" x="285" y="51" text-anchor="middle">Discover</text>
          <text class="s2" x="285" y="66" text-anchor="middle">SOURCES</text>
          <path class="a2" d="M330,56 L348,56" marker-end="url(#arr2)"></path>

          <rect class="n2" x="350" y="30" width="86" height="52" rx="8"></rect>
          <text class="t2" x="393" y="51" text-anchor="middle">Filter</text>
          <text class="s2" x="393" y="66" text-anchor="middle">ELIGIBILITY</text>
          <path class="a2" d="M436,56 L454,56" marker-end="url(#arr2)"></path>

          <rect class="n2" x="456" y="30" width="90" height="52" rx="8"></rect>
          <text class="t2" x="501" y="51" text-anchor="middle">Verify</text>
          <text class="s2" x="501" y="66" text-anchor="middle">SOURCE PAGES</text>
          <path class="a2" d="M546,56 L564,56" marker-end="url(#arr2)"></path>

          <rect class="n2" x="566" y="4" width="104" height="48" rx="8"></rect>
          <text class="t2" x="618" y="24" text-anchor="middle">Record</text>
          <text class="s2" x="618" y="39" text-anchor="middle">CSV HISTORY</text>
          <path class="a2" d="M618,52 L618,66" marker-end="url(#arr2)" display="none"></path>

          <rect class="n2" x="566" y="62" width="104" height="48" rx="8"></rect>
          <text class="t2" x="618" y="82" text-anchor="middle">Report</text>
          <text class="s2" x="618" y="97" text-anchor="middle">DATED, ACTIONABLE</text>

          <rect class="n2" x="566" y="130" width="104" height="44" rx="8"></rect>
          <text class="t2" x="618" y="149" text-anchor="middle">Discord</text>
          <text class="s2" x="618" y="163" text-anchor="middle">DELIVERY</text>
          <path class="a2" d="M618,110 L618,128" marker-end="url(#arr2)"></path>

          <path class="a2" d="M501,82 C501,150 560,152 564,152" stroke-dasharray="4 4" marker-end="url(#arr2)"></path>
          <rect class="b2" x="380" y="130" width="170" height="44" rx="8"></rect>
          <text class="t2" x="465" y="149" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8A6D3B">Unverified / access blocked</text>
          <text class="s2" x="465" y="163" text-anchor="middle">MARKED — NOT COUNTED AS VERIFIED</text>
        </svg>
        <p class="caption">CONCEPTUAL, SANITIZED WORKFLOW</p>
      </div>

      <h2>Outcome</h2>
      <p>
        The workflow produced 12 consecutive weekly reports, built a 127-entry structured history,
        and identified 18 individually verified opportunities in its most recent audited report.
        This demonstrates continuity, filtering, and validation in one private workflow. It does
        not demonstrate commercial customer adoption or guaranteed job placements.
      </p>

      <h2>What I would improve</h2>
      <p>
        Add stronger health checks, an exception queue for blocked sources, structured retry
        policy, per-source error rates, and a lightweight "review needed" state for uncertain
        findings.
      </p>

      <div class="limits">
        <h3>Limits and disclosure</h3>
        <p>
          Private single-beneficiary workflow operated on internal infrastructure. Beneficiary
          identity, real contact data, private reports, and scraped material are not published.
        </p>
      </div>

      <EvidencePanel />
    </div>

    <nav class="case-nav" aria-label="Case study navigation">
      <a href="/work/ai-agent-operations/">← Previous: Making multi-agent work accountable</a>
      <a href="/work/research-validation/">Next: Designing research to reject weak conclusions →</a>
    </nav>
  </div>

  <ContactCTA />
</BaseLayout>
